om Desulfonispora thiosulfatigenes: purification, properties and primary sequence. Biochem J 357:581–586\nL102: \nL103: 【36†[Google Scholar]†scholar.google.com】\nL104:   10. Denger K., Weinitschke S., Hollemeyer K., Cook A. M. 2004; Sulfoacetate generated by Rhodopseudomonas palustris from taurine. Arch Microbiol 182:254–258\nL105: 【37†[Google Scholar]†scholar.google.com】\nL106:   11. Denger K., Smits T. H. M., Cook A. M. 2006; l-Cysteate sulpho-lyase, a widespread, pyridoxal5′-phosphate-coupled desulphonative enzyme purified from Silicibacter pomeroyi DSS-3^{T} . Biochem J 394:657–664\nL107: 【38†[Google Scholar]†scholar.google.com】\nL108:   12. Denger K., Weinitschke S., Smits T. H. M., Schleheck D., Cook A. M. 2008; Bacterial sulfite dehydrogenases in organotrophic metabolism: separation and identification in Cupriavidus necator H16 and in Delftia acidovorans SPH-1. Microbiology 154:256–263\nL109: 【39†[Google Scholar]†scholar.google.com】\nL110:   13. Denger K., Mayer J., Buhmann M., Weinitschke S., Smits T. H. M., Cook A. M. 2009; Bifurcated degradative pathway of 3-sulfolactate in Roseovarius nubinhibens ISM via sulfoacetaldehyde acetyltransferase and ( S)-cysteate sulfo-lyase. J Bacteriol 191:5648–5656\nL111: 【40†[Google Scholar]†scholar.google.com】\nL112:   14. Folkers K., Koniuszy F., Shavel J. 1944; Erythrina alkaloids. XIV. Isolation and characterization of erysothiovine and erysothiopine, new alkaloids containing sulfur. J Am Chem Soc 66:1083–1087\nL113: \nL114: 【41†[Google Scholar]†scholar.google.com】\nL115:   15. Graham D. E., White R. H. 2002; Elucidation of methanogenic coenzyme biosyntheses: from spectroscopy to genomics. Nat Prod Rep 19:133–147\nL116: 【42†[Google Scholar]†scholar.google.com】\nL117:   16. Graupner M., Xu H., White R. H. 2000; Identification of an archaeal 2-hydroxy acid dehydrogenase catalyzing reactions involved in coenzyme biosynthesis in methanoarchaea. J Bacteriol 182:3688–3692\nL118: \nL119: 【43†[Google Scholar]†scholar.google.com